{"metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"HTTPDestination"}],"modules":[{"name":"HTTPDestinations"}],"externalID":"s:16HTTPDestinations15HTTPDestinationV","title":"HTTPDestination","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"HTTPDestination","kind":"identifier"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"HTTPDestination.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination.swift#L78"},"roleHeading":"Structure"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A destination that sends each batch it receives to an HTTP endpoint, as the requests its encoder"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"splits it into, and sends each again until it arrives."}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/init(endpoint:headerFields:instrument:encoder:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/init(endpoint:headerFields:instrument:transport:encoder:backoff:clock:)"],"title":"Initializers","generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/dropReports"],"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/receive(_:)"],"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/Destination-Implementations"],"title":"Default Implementations","generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport"],"title":"Sending batches","generated":true,"anchor":"Sending-batches"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"HTTPDestination","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Transport","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Encoding","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Transport","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations13HTTPTransportP","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport","text":"HTTPTransport","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Encoding","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations12BatchEncoderP","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","text":"BatchEncoder","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The wire shape, for a server that ingests these batches:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The requests the encoder splits each batch into ("},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"), in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order the delivery hands batches over, each request sent only once the previous one is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivered or dropped."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The method is ","type":"text"},{"code":"POST","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the URL is the configured endpoint.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The header fields are the configured ones, then the trace context of the request’s first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record, then "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Content-Type"},{"type":"text","text":", each replacing fields of the same name before it:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The instrument injects the first (oldest) record’s "},{"code":"EventRecord\/context","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so a server"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"extracting it joins the request, and the events, to the trace the app was in. Its field"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"names are the instrument’s: "},{"code":"traceparent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"tracestate","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for a W3C Trace Context tracer."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A record tracked outside any span, or an instrument that injects nothing (the default"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"NoOpInstrument","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when none is bootstrapped), adds no fields."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Only the first record’s context travels in the header fields, though a request may hold","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"records tracked in other traces. A server that needs each record’s context reads it from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the body, where a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" writes it.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Content-Type"},{"type":"text","text":" is always the encoder’s "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedBatch\/contentType"},{"type":"text","text":", whatever a configured"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"field or the instrument wrote."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The body is exactly the encoder’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedBatch\/body","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" for the request’s records, oldest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"first. The format is the encoder’s; events need no ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"text":" conformance.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A response with a 2xx status means the batch arrived.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A request the transport can never send ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransportError\/invalidRequest(reason:)"},{"type":"text","text":": a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"malformed or unsupported URL, or an "},{"code":"http","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" URL App Transport Security refuses) isn’t sent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No response, a 5xx status, 408 Request Timeout or 429 Too Many Requests means it didn’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"arrive yet: the same request is sent again after the backoff’s next wait, for as long as it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"takes. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Retry-After"},{"type":"text","text":" field is not read; the backoff alone sets the wait."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Any other status means the endpoint won’t take the request, and it isn’t sent again. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"batch’s later requests are still sent."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A record can arrive twice: a request the server took whose response was lost is sent","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"again, and a record a store redelivers after the app was stopped mid-send","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord\/isRedelivered","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") may have arrived before. Its ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord\/id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the one it was","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"first sent with, so an encoder that writes each record’s identifier lets the server keep one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"copy.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A batch of several requests is acknowledged only once every request is delivered or dropped."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A delivery cancelled, or an app stopped, after some of its requests arrived hands the whole"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"batch over again, so those requests are sent again too: a server that keeps one copy per"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record identifier absorbs them. The records the encoder leaves out are then reported again."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/receive(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" returns once the batch is delivered, dropped, or the delivery is cancelled, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a tracker’s store keeps the records of a batch until it arrives, and a batch still being"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"retried when the app ends is delivered again on the next launch. A request the endpoint"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rejects or that can’t be sent, a batch the encoder can’t encode, and a record the encoder"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"leaves out of its requests are dropped: logged at error level and reported on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/dropReports","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". Each failed attempt that will be retried is logged at notice level."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Cancelling the delivery cancels the send in flight or the wait before the next one, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/receive(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" returns without logging or reporting it, or sending the batch’s later"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"requests. A request whose wait before the next attempt throws something other than"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"CancellationError","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (a custom clock’s failure) is given up on, logged at error level but not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reported, and the batch’s next request is sent."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"While a batch is retried, the delivery’s later batches wait in this destination’s buffer,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which drops its oldest batch when full and reports it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deliver(to:batchBufferLimit:bufferDropReporter:)"},{"type":"text","text":"). With a store, a dropped batch’s records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"aren’t lost: once this destination has caught up, the delivery reads them back from the store"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and hands them to it again, in the same run, so they are sent once the endpoint answers."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Without a store, the records of a dropped batch are lost."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let collector = HTTPDestination(","    endpoint: collectorURL,","    headerFields: [.authorization: \"Bearer \\(token)\"],","    encoder: PlansEncoder())","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: collector)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination"]}],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"HTTPDestination","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"HTTPDestination","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"HTTPDestination","abstract":[{"text":"A destination that sends each batch it receives to an HTTP endpoint, as the requests its encoder","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"splits it into, and sends each again until it arrives.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","type":"topic"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/BatchEncoder":{"kind":"s